WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.387
Let's follow Alex's birthday enquiry through the latest FormBridge guided demo. The

00:00:04.387 --> 00:00:08.775
page shows whose turn it is, brings the current step into view,

00:00:08.775 --> 00:00:11.700
and keeps the next action at the bottom.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:17.659
Start as Alex. Press Tab in the empty message box, or select

00:00:17.659 --> 00:00:22.968
Fill guest message. The suggestion includes the restaurant, date, time, guest count

00:00:22.968 --> 00:00:26.950
and special requests. Send the enquiry to the team.

00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:32.891
FormBridge extracts the five booking details and saves the enquiry in the

00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:37.300
separate demo inbox. The original message stays with the brief.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:43.461
Now Alex changes the plans. Fill the correction and update the enquiry.

00:00:43.461 --> 00:00:48.972
The restaurant and date stay in place, while the guest count and

00:00:48.972 --> 00:00:50.350
time preference change.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:56.725
The demo switches to the host and shows Staff's turn. Suggest eight-thirty

00:00:56.725 --> 00:01:02.450
and add the staff reply. An offer still needs the guest's acceptance.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:08.676
Switch back to Alex. Fill and send the acceptance. Only now can

00:01:08.676 --> 00:01:11.000
eight-thirty become the agreed time.

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:17.650
Open Time in the brief. Staff can inspect the offer and the

00:01:17.650 --> 00:01:23.650
acceptance, alongside earlier messages. The change history keeps the previous request visible.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:29.944
Find guest requests. Read the quotations, then select the birthday, quiet table

00:01:29.944 --> 00:01:35.589
and dietary request. Staff still need to confirm dietary requirements with the

00:01:35.589 --> 00:01:37.000
guest and kitchen.

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:42.294
Check the brief and fill the handoff note. Approve and save. The

00:01:42.294 --> 00:01:46.939
enquiry now has a reviewed request, an owner and a follow-up time

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:48.100
for the team.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:54.490
Create the guest review link. Check the details as Alex, tick the

00:01:54.490 --> 00:02:00.230
confirmation box and send the review back. The guest view keeps staff

00:02:00.230 --> 00:02:03.100
notes and the full conversation private.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:09.958
Return to the host. Check the simulated availability, review the returned times,

00:02:09.958 --> 00:02:16.165
then complete the simulated handoff. This demonstration does not contact a real

00:02:16.165 --> 00:02:17.200
reservation platform.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:23.010
The tour is complete. The guest's changing plans, their reviewed requests and

00:02:23.010 --> 00:02:28.170
the next step are together in one enquiry. Open the guided demo

00:02:28.170 --> 00:02:30.750
to try the same workflow yourself.
